# Section 5: D3 Test Quality — folded TAP-1…4 (WI-4)

The deprecated `docs/reviews/TDD_AGENTS_MD_REVIEW.md` testing anti-patterns now
live here, cited from the nested `AGENTS.md` test sections:

- **TAP-1 (tautological tests)** — the test reimplements the production algorithm
  (e.g. computing SHA-256 in the test to compare against `compute_signature()`).
  *Detection: LLM (an AST heuristic — test re-imports the impl symbol it asserts
  on — may be provided deterministically).* Severity: warning.
- **TAP-2 (mock addiction)** — more than 3 mocks in one test. *Detection: AST
  (mock-count).* Severity: warning.
- **TAP-3 (determinism theater)** — asserting exact LLM output strings at
  `temperature=0`. *Detection: LLM.* Severity: warning.
- **TAP-4 (gap blindness)** — a decision point (gate/guard) has an acceptance
  test but no rejection test; write the rejection test first. *Detection: AST
  (failure-test ratio per decision point).* Severity: warning.

When deterministic TAP results are provided, defer to them; otherwise judge with
calibrated confidence.

